there's an art to finding the right  actor for a role and sometimes  filmmakers need to see what they don't  want before they're able to settle on  what they do it's easy to imagine that  the stars who play our favorite film  characters were the first and only  people considered that's not always the  case  hard as it might be to believe these  iconic roles could have easily ended up  in different hands Stuart Townsend as  Aragorn everyone is familiar with Viggo  Mortensen's captivating portrayal of  Aragorn a ranger of the north and  eventual king of Gondor and the lord of  the rings as great as he is Mortensen  actually scooped the role from Stuart  Townsend who spent two months training  before he was let go  Townsend would go on to his own  successes but he didn't look back on his  brush with middle-earth fondly telling  Entertainment Weekly I did get shafted I  was there rehearsing and training for  two months and was fired the day before  filming began that's some Sauron level  treachery right there Sean Connery as  Gandalf  yes Peter Jackson and his team  originally intended for crotchety Sean  Connery to play Gandalf the Grey but  Connery refused it's not the first big  role Connery turned down either other  rejected roles include Dumbledore from  the Harry Potter series John Hammond  from Jurassic Park and Morpheus in the  matrix as far as the Lord of the Rings  casting went he told the New Zealand  Herald I never understood it I read the  book I read the script I saw the movie I  still don't understand it I would be  interested in doing something that I  didn't fully understand but not for 18  months luckily we ended up with Sir Ian  McKellen as the lovable wizard and  static Will Smith as Django the list of  r-rated movie starring Will Smith is  pretty short but despite this he was  originally written in as the hero in  Django Unchained he didn't pass on the  movie just to maintain his wholesome  image however Smith revealed to  Entertainment Weekly that he didn't want  to play the character after finding out  that he wasn't originally going to be  playing the lead or going to be killing  the bad guy after The Fresh Prince  passed Django became the lead character  anyway with Christoph Waltz's dr. King  Schultz stepping aside for Jamie Foxx to  take the spotlight sorry well Robert  Downey jr. as lieutenant Matthew  Kowalski when we think about Robert  Downey jr. these days we tend to picture  his head stuck in the Iron Man helmet a  picture Tony Stark a Sandra Bullock's  co-star at gravity as he told Howard  Stern down he passed on the role because  he just couldn't stand this  special effects rug that he was strapped  into coincidentally Scarlett Johansson  was also a potential candidate for  Bullock's role  we're pretty sure two Avengers could  have made it back from space with no  problems but then again there's only so  many times we can see Downey floating  helplessly in space Chris Farley as  Shrek Mike Myers performance as the  lovable ogre helped make Shrek an  instant classic but prior to Myers  voicing the green guy a large portion of  the film's dialogue was recorded by  Chris Farley aah help a big stupid  stinky smelly ugly ogre I'm so scared  his untimely death in 1997 derailed  production resulting in major delays  luckily Shrek was able to find a  suitable voice courtesy of Farley's  friend and former Saturday Night Live  cast mate meg Ryan Diane Lane and  Michelle Pfeiffer as Vivian Ward pretty  woman pretty much launched Julia Roberts  career but she only got the role of the  hooker with a heart of gold after a  bunch of bigger names past first  director Garry Marshall originally had  meg Ryan lined up to play the part of  Vivian Ward after she departed the  project Diane Lane got as far as costume  fittings before dropping out Michelle  Pfeiffer caught Marshalls eye which he  also declined the role leaving them the  hands of the relatively unknown Roberts  who was just 21 at the time it turned  out that she was the perfect person to  fall in love with Richard Gere on screen  and sell a truckload of Roxette Records  along the way Meryl Streep as Ellen  Ripley Sigourney Weaver Brooks cinematic  barriers of female badassery and the  Alien franchise but the production team  originally had its eye on Meryl Streep  for the role of Ellen Ripley  the actress dropped out prior to the  start of production because of the death  of her boyfriend  Godfather actor John Cazale upon  Streep's exit Scott briefly turned to  Veronica Carr tried to play Ripley and  then switch things up again giving the  role to Weaver Cartwright was instead  given the part of chief navigator  Lambert several decades in classic films  later it's obvious he made the right  choice Oh J Simpson as the Terminator  surprisingly our own Swardson Edgar had  a Juke past a football great to score  the role of the unrelenting t800 cyborg  at the 1984 sci-fi classic The  Terminator Entertainment Weekly reported  that Orion Pictures co-founder Mike  Medavoy wanted Oh Jay Simpson to star of  the Terminator saying at the time OJ  Simpson how one of those commercials for  Hertz were he jumped over a counter and  ran to get a rental car it was all of  that athletic stuff which I thought the  Terminator should  have Medavoy was so set on having  Simpson as the t800 that he offered  Schwarzenegger the role of Kyle Reese  which would ultimately be played by  Michael Biehn thankfully common sense  intervened or maybe it was Skynet Bill  Murray as Batman by the time Michael  Keaton donned the Caped Crusader's cowl  another take on the character had  already spent years in development an  earlier project simply called the Batman  had stalled due to the deaths of a few  potential casting choices and director  Ivan Reitman took the reins in his new  version he initially wanted Bill Murray  to play Batman with Eddie Murphy as  Robin when you think about Keaton's  Bruce Wayne the idea of Bill Murray in  the part doesn't seem all that  far-fetched  except maybe picturing him the Batsuit  eventually Warner Brothers handed the  reins to Tim Burton who acts the Batman  script completely and gave us the 1989  Batman we all know and love everyone in  ghostbusters believe it or not Paul  pee-wee Herman Reubens was originally  intended to play gozer the gozerian at  the end of ghostbusters that's just one  of the many ways in which the 1984  comedy horror classic changed during its  journey to the screen dan Aykroyd who  wrote the script with meatballs in  Animal House vet Harold Ramis originally  envisioned a futuristic time-traveling  adventure starring himself and fellow  blues brother and SNL pal John Belushi  understanding that the original concept  would have made ghostbusters too  expensive to film Ramos helped reshape  the story but Belushi's untimely death  in 1982 threw a wrench into development  the movie was eventually rewritten into  the ensemble story we know and love with  Belushi there in spirit too according to  director Ivan Reitman the glowing green  ghost known as Slimer was conceived as a  tribute to Belushi it's not hard to tell  how Ramos and Aykroyd also wanted John  Candy to star as Louis Tully but candy  passed on the project the role  eventually went to Rick Moranis to top  things off before Ernie Hudson joined  the cast as winston zeddemore Aykroyd  originally wanted his Trading Places  co-star Eddie Murphy for the role Murphy  had to pass because he was shooting  Beverly Hills Cop but that's alright  because Ernie Hudson loves this town  just about everyone as Sam wheat despite  the wishes of ghost writer Bruce Joel  Rubin who wanted the role of Sam wheat  to go to Patrick Swayze director Jerry  Zucker went through a slew of noteworthy  actors - stars the film's death lothario  according to IMDB some of the names who  turned down the film's title role  include Johnny Depp Kevin Bacon Nicolas  Cage Kevin Costner Tom Cruise Harrison  Ford Mel Gibson Tom Hanks John Travolta  and Alec Baldwin even Bruce Willis who  was married to go star Demi Moore at the  time passed on the project eventually  Zucker came around to Ruben's way of  thinking which was definitely for the  past we really couldn't imagine any more  supernatural scenes with Nick Cave  thanks for watching subscribe to our  YouTube channel to watch more videos  like the one you just saw and leave us a  comment to let us know which alternate  actors you would have liked you've seen  in these walls
 

